      "id": "aoebixq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industries are systematically classified based on raw material source, size, ownership, and product nature.",
        "The location of industries is determined by geographical factors like raw materials, power, and water, as well as non-geographical factors like market, labor, capital, and government policy.",
        "India features eight major industrial clusters, including the Mumbai-Pune, Hugli, Bengaluru-Tamil Nadu, and Chota Nagpur regions.",
        "The New Industrial Policy of 1991 transformed Indian manufacturing through Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization (LPG).",
        "Major manufacturing industries in India include iron and steel, cotton textiles, sugar, petrochemicals, and information technology."
      ],
      "id": "g590l46"
